<title>GERMANY: CSFB upgrades Hoechst to buy from hold.</title>
<headline>CSFB upgrades Hoechst to buy from hold.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Suisse first Boston said it had upgraded Hoechst to &quot;buy&quot; from &quot;hold&quot; and set a target price for the share of 90 marks.</p>
<p>Hoechst was trading stronger at 76.50 marks at 0800 GMT, up 2.60 marks from Monday.</p>
<p>Dealers said the CSFB upgrade followed a similar move by Salomon Brothers which had been released to the market on Monday. They said the changes followed a positive outlook for the company presented by Hoechst chairman Juergen Dormann at an event in London this week.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
